---@class posthog.llm_skills.LlmSkillsNamePublishCommunityCreateRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field skill_name string
---@field expected_skill_id string Immutable ID of the skill version that the publisher reviewed.
---@field expected_version number Skill version that the publisher reviewed. The request returns 409 if the latest version changed.
---@field expected_category? string Category of the skill the publisher reviewed. Registering a skill as a scout changes its category without raising its version, so the version alone would let a skill reviewed as an ordinary one publish as a scout. The request returns 409 if the category changed. Omit it to skip that check.
---@field scout_config? posthog.llm_skills.CommunitySkillScoutConfig Schedule, emit posture and tags to publish alongside a scout, so it arrives in another project with its cadence intact. Rejected for a skill that is not a scout.
---@field display_name? string Human-friendly display name for the community listing. Defaults to a title-cased skill slug. Must be a single line: it is used as the pull request title and commit message.
---@field tags? posthog.llm_skills.LlmSkillsNamePublishCommunityCreateRequestTagsList Tags used for filtering and discovery in the marketplace, e.g. ['web-analytics', 'triage'].
---@field author_handle? string The publisher's GitHub username, used for public attribution on the listing and PR. Optional, and self-reported: it is not verified against the publisher's PostHog account.

---Tags used for filtering and discovery in the marketplace, e.g. ['web-analytics', 'triage'].
---@alias posthog.llm_skills.LlmSkillsNamePublishCommunityCreateRequestTagsList string[]

