---@class posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field skill_name string
---@field body? string Full skill body (SKILL.md instruction content) to publish as a new version. Mutually exclusive with edits.
---@field edits? posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestEditsList List of find/replace operations to apply to the current skill body. Each edit's 'old' text must match exactly once. Edits are applied sequentially. Mutually exclusive with body.
---@field description? string Updated description for the new version.
---@field license? string License name or reference.
---@field compatibility? string Environment requirements.
---@field allowed_tools? posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestAllowedToolsList Tools the skill asks to use. Tool names cannot contain whitespace. A harness that reads the skill from a file (zip export, git marketplace, a content=full bundle) treats the list as pre-approved. A harness that loads the skill over MCP, including the default content=stub bundle, ignores the list until the user approves that grant.
---@field metadata? posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestMetadataMap Arbitrary key-value metadata.
---@field files? posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestFilesList Bundled files to include with this version. Replaces all files from the previous version. Mutually exclusive with file_edits.
---@field file_edits? posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestFileEditsList Per-file find/replace updates. Each entry targets one existing file by path and applies sequential edits to its content. Non-targeted files carry forward unchanged. Cannot add, remove, or rename files — use 'files' for that. Mutually exclusive with files.
---@field owners? posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestOwnersList Replace the skill's owners with these user UUIDs (each a member of this project). Omit to leave owners unchanged; pass an empty list to clear them. Owners are keyed on the logical skill, so setting them is independent of the version being published — a body edit alone never changes ownership.
---@field base_version? number Latest version you are editing from. Used for optimistic concurrency checks. Required when publishing content changes; optional for an owner-only update (when omitted, owners are replaced without a concurrency check).
---@field version_description? string Optional note describing what changed in this version. Shown in the version history.

---Tools the skill asks to use. Tool names cannot contain whitespace. A harness that reads the skill from a file (zip export, git marketplace, a content=full bundle) treats the list as pre-approved. A harness that loads the skill over MCP, including the default content=stub bundle, ignores the list until the user approves that grant.
---@alias posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestAllowedToolsList string[]

---List of find/replace operations to apply to the current skill body. Each edit's 'old' text must match exactly once. Edits are applied sequentially. Mutually exclusive with body.
---@alias posthog.llm_skills.UpdateLlmSkillsNamePartialRequestEditsList posthog.llm_skills.LLMSkillEditOperation[]

---Per-file find/replace updates. Each entry targets one existing file by path and applies sequential edits to its content. Non-targeted files carry forward unchanged. Cannot add, remove, or rename files — use 'files' for that. Mutually exclusive with files.
